findings[5]:
  - confidence: high
    id: RF-001
    limitations: "The Agent Skills specification does not define an executable DAG, so the v4 manifest remains an AI SDLC extension."
    source_ids[4]: SRC-001,SRC-002,SRC-003,SRC-007
    statement: The canonical skill router should stay concise while a machine-readable DAG selects focused step documents and references just in time.
    trace_targets[4]: FR-001,FR-002,NFR-001,DEC-002
  - confidence: high
    id: RF-002
    limitations: Filesystem journaling is suitable for the portable local harness but does not replace a transactional distributed scheduler.
    source_ids[3]: SRC-004,SRC-006,SRC-007
    statement: "Resume safety requires stable task identity, persisted results, deterministic dependency order, TOON-serializable state, idempotency keys, and explicit side-effect boundaries."
    trace_targets[4]: FR-004,FR-005,NFR-002,DEC-003
  - confidence: high
    id: RF-003
    limitations: Lexical retrieval trades semantic recall for offline determinism; live evals must guard representative cases where wording differs.
    source_ids[3]: SRC-003,SRC-004,SRC-007
    statement: "Context should be compiled per step from mandatory anchors plus deterministic lexical topology and trace signals, with sufficiency and recall gates before execution."
    trace_targets[4]: FR-003,NFR-003,NFR-004,DEC-004
  - confidence: high
    id: RF-004
    limitations: Live-agent quality varies by host and provider; the repository can define a neutral protocol but cannot certify every external runtime offline.
    source_ids[3]: SRC-002,SRC-005,SRC-007
    statement: "A maintainable harness needs repository-native contracts, generated projections, drift checks, deterministic evals for every skill, and a separate live-agent evaluation tier."
    trace_targets[4]: FR-006,FR-007,NFR-005,DEC-005
  - confidence: high
    id: RF-005
    limitations: This is an AI SDLC policy choice derived from the repository safety model rather than a universal external requirement.
    source_ids[4]: SRC-004,SRC-005,SRC-006,SRC-007
    statement: Explore must remain read-only and durable run creation must begin only at Apply so planning probes cannot leave hidden execution state.
    trace_targets[3]: FR-005,NFR-006,DEC-006
open_questions[1]{id,next_action,owner,question}:
  OQ-001,Run the provider-neutral live eval protocol on the release candidate and record provider-specific receipts without changing deterministic core behavior.,Release maintainers,Which provider and model matrix should be required for the first live v4 release certification?
questions[4]:
  - id: RQ-001
    question: Which skill structure makes multi-step agent work explicit without loading every instruction eagerly?
    trace_targets[4]: FR-001,FR-002,NFR-001,DEC-002
  - id: RQ-002
    question: "Which durable-execution invariants are required for safe resume, retry, and side effects?"
    trace_targets[4]: FR-004,FR-005,NFR-002,DEC-003
  - id: RQ-003
    question: How should context be selected and measured for long-running skill steps?
    trace_targets[4]: FR-003,NFR-003,NFR-004,DEC-004
  - id: RQ-004
    question: Which repository and evaluation feedback loops make an agent harness maintainable?
    trace_targets[4]: FR-006,FR-007,NFR-005,DEC-005
schema: ai-sdlc-research-input/v1
scope: mixed
sources[7]{accessed_at,credibility,id,locator,notes,title,type}:
  2026-07-30,Canonical Agent Skills format specification.,SRC-001,"https://agentskills.io/specification","Defines progressive disclosure, skill directory structure, validation, and concise SKILL.md guidance.",Agent Skills specification,open-specification
  2026-07-30,Official Agent Skills authoring guidance.,SRC-002,"https://agentskills.io/skill-creation/best-practices","Recommends explicit checklists, dependency and validation gates, moderate detail, and on-demand references.",Best practices for skill creators,official-guidance
  2026-07-30,Primary engineering publication from an agent platform provider.,SRC-003,"https://www.anthropic.com/engineering/effective-context-engineering-for-ai-agents","Treats context as a finite attention budget and recommends high-signal just-in-time retrieval, compaction, and structured memory.",Effective context engineering for AI agents,engineering-research
  2026-07-30,Primary report describing a tested long-running coding harness.,SRC-004,"https://www.anthropic.com/engineering/effective-harnesses-for-long-running-agents","Reports better continuity from incremental work, explicit progress artifacts, clean handoffs, and feature-by-feature execution.",Effective harnesses for long-running agents,engineering-experiment
  2026-07-30,Primary OpenAI engineering case study.,SRC-005,"https://openai.com/index/harness-engineering/","Uses repository knowledge as the system of record and emphasizes legibility, executable feedback loops, and architecture enforcement.","Harness engineering: leveraging Codex in an agent-first world",engineering-case-study
  2026-07-30,Official durable workflow runtime documentation.,SRC-006,"https://docs.langchain.com/oss/javascript/langgraph/functional-api","Specifies checkpointed task results, TOON-serializable state, deterministic replay order, idempotency, and encapsulated side effects.","LangGraph functional API: durable execution",runtime-documentation
  2026-07-30,Direct source-code inspection and baseline test execution in this repository.,SRC-007,skills/ai-sdlc-shared-runtime,"Shows v1 three-step manifests, v3 context packs, plan-only workflow graphs, durable run primitives, and contract drift.","Current AI SDLC Harness runtime, step, context, flow, and skill contracts",internal-evidence
topic: Deterministic executable skill harness and context engineering for AI SDLC Harness v4
